  "notes": [
    "The 10-Q reports rounded ounces and pounds sold. Use its reported sales amounts as historical controls and check rounded price × volume within unit precision. Exact accounting waterfall totals are reported in USD millions.",
    "Q4 uses the latest complete October monthly benchmark by metal as a quarter-average proxy. The source measures precious metals in USD per troy ounce and base metals in USD per metric tonne. November 12 is the evidence cutoff. The October monthly observation is neither a November closing price nor Newmont's realized Q4 price.",
    "Use the World Bank 2027 annual forecast as an independent nominal market-price input. Newmont's commodity assumptions are for its 2026 cost outlook and do not constitute realized sales price guidance. The Newmont earnings release's lead equivalent in USD/lb differs from its rounded metric table. This file preserves the stated cost-guidance footnote of $0.90/lb.",
    "Forecast realization uses the ratio of Newmont's September-quarter gross realized price to the matched benchmark, after applying the physical silver stream to the benchmark for silver. Gross is before provisional remeasurement, the noncash streaming-liability amortization and treatment or refining adjustments.",
    "At September 30, the company reported no instruments designated to hedge metals prices. Disclosed cash-flow hedges cover foreign exchange and Cadia power purchase costs. Provisional concentrate sales remain subject to settlement. A zero incremental provisional mark is a neutral modeling assumption. Q4 settlement prices and the net amount of prior-shipment marks are unobserved.",
    "The retained stream revenue amortization is a noncash item, and future cash flow should remove it once. Apply any stream price discount only once in projected gross realized prices. Positive copper treatment and refining adjustment reflects the reported sign; future terms are unobserved and the model uses the trailing reported adjustment as a proxy."
  ]
}
